report: "---\nauthor: \"builder\"\ncreated: \"2026-11-23\"\nupdated: \"2026-11-23\"\n---\n\n# Flip the private workspaces on llm to public\n\nProject: endojs/endo-but-for-bots. Branch: `llm-flip-private-public`. The\nsame commits are also on the job branch `job/endo-llm-flip-private-public/3`.\n\nBase commit: `0368767778a232c38721ff8a1e88d8f68272624d` (llm's tip in the\ncheckout; the pinned snapshot is `llm-0368767`). The pull request should be\nopened against `llm-0368767`. Nothing was rebased.\n\nCommits, oldest first:\n\n- `a035fc31b` chore: make private workspaces public on llm for dev releases\n- `5353c8d77` fix: make newly public workspaces pack to complete tarballs\n- `a482cf2bd` build: give newly public workspaces a local typescript\n- `8622e2f7d` chore: add changeset for workspaces made public on llm\n\n## Pull request\n\nTitle: `chore: make private workspaces public on llm for dev releases`\n\nDescription:\n\n> This makes 55 workspaces public on `llm`, so the garden can publish them to\n> npm.minion.town as `dev-*` prereleases. The maintainer asked for this.\n>\n> Base: `0368767778a232c38721ff8a1e88d8f68272624d` (`llm-0368767`).\n>\n> **Why this is safe on llm.** These workspaces stay private on the endo\n> repository's `master` branch, and `llm` is never merged there as a whole, so\n> this change cannot make them public upstream by accident.\n>\n> **History.** `@endo/daemon` and `@endo/cli` were made private upstream in\n> 986af720a (Erik Marks, 2024-02-15, \"feat(cli,daemon): Make packages private\"),\n> \"to prevent accidentally publishing @endo/daemon and @endo/cli\". This reverses\n> that on `llm` only.\n>\n> **What changes.** Each flipped workspace drops `\"private\": true` and has\n> `publishConfig.access: public` (most already had it). Packing all 55 showed\n> five more fixes were needed:\n>\n> - 27 workspaces had no `typescript` devDependency. ts-node-pack runs\n>   `yarn bin tsc` in the workspace and otherwise falls back to `npx tsc`,\n>   which fetches the unrelated `tsc` package and fails. They now take\n>   `typescript` from the dev catalog (`yarn.lock` updated).\n> - `@endo/cli`: `files` did not include `bin/`, so the `endo` executable\n>   was missing from the tarball.\n> - `@endo/lal`: `files` did not include `providers/`, which\n>   `./providers/index.js` exports.\n> - `@endo/sandbox` and `@endo/reminder`: a types-only subpath was a bare\n>   string pointing at a `.d.ts`, which ts-node-pack rewrites to a missing\n>   `.d.js`. It is now `{ \"types\": \"./src/types.d.ts\" }`, as\n>   `@endo/ocapn-noise` and `@endo/ocapn` already do.\n> - `@endo/pubsub`: its exports had `types` conditions naming `.d.ts`\n>   files that nothing emits under ts-node-pack (the package has no `.ts`\n>   sources). The conditions are removed; the exports are plain `.js` paths.\n>\n> A changeset gives each flipped workspace a `patch` entry.\n>\n> ### Made public\n>\n> | Package | Path | Version |\n> | --- | --- | --- |\n> | `@endo/9p-server` | `packages/9p-server` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/agent-mcp-stdio` | `packages/agent-mcp-stdio` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/chat` | `packages/chat` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/claude-sandbox` | `packages/claude-sandbox` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/claude` | `packages/claude` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/cli` | `packages/cli` | 2.3.13 |\n> | `@endo/codex-sandbox` | `packages/codex-sandbox` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/conversation-tree` | `packages/conversation-tree` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/daemon-cas` | `packages/daemon-cas` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/daemon` | `packages/daemon` | 2.5.3 |\n> | `@endo/endo-fs-asset-server` | `packages/endo-fs-asset-server` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/endo-fs-exec` | `packages/endo-fs-exec` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/exo-npm` | `packages/exo-npm` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/exo-package-manager` | `packages/exo-package-manager` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/exo-unzip` | `packages/exo-unzip` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/exo-zip` | `packages/exo-zip` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/fae` | `packages/fae` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/fetch` | `packages/fetch` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/floot` | `packages/floot` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/gateway` | `packages/gateway` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/git` | `packages/git` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/goblin-chat` | `packages/goblin-chat` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/host-shell` | `packages/host-shell` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/host-spawner` | `packages/host-spawner` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/hosted-agent` | `packages/hosted-agent` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/ironhorse-prelude` | `packages/ironhorse-prelude` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/jaine` | `packages/jaine` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/jsonl-transcript` | `packages/jsonl-transcript` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/lal` | `packages/lal` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/mem-cas` | `packages/mem-cas` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/monaco-wrapper` | `packages/monaco-wrapper` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/npm-registry-server` | `packages/npm-registry-server` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/ocapn-iroh` | `packages/ocapn-iroh` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/ocapn-noise` | `packages/ocapn-noise` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/opencode-sandbox` | `packages/opencode-sandbox` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/preact-container` | `packages/preact-container` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/preact-social` | `packages/preact-social` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/pubsub` | `packages/pubsub` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/relay-server` | `packages/relay-server` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/reminder` | `packages/reminder` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/sandbox` | `packages/sandbox` | 0.0.1 |\n> | `@endo/space-channel` | `packages/space-channel` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-chat` | `packages/space-chat` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-endo-mgmt` | `packages/space-endo-mgmt` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-file-explorer` | `packages/space-file-explorer` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-floot` | `packages/space-floot` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-inventory-graph` | `packages/space-inventory-graph` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-nixos-admin` | `packages/space-nixos-admin` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-peers` | `packages/space-peers` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-whylip` | `packages/space-whylip` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/space-workflow` | `packages/space-workflow` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/spaces-util` | `packages/spaces-util` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/thixotrope` | `packages/thixotrope` | 0.1.0 |\n> | `@endo/workflow` | `packages/workflow` | 0.0.0 |\n> | `@endo/x402` | `packages/x402` | 1.0.0 |\n>\n> All versions are plain `x.y.z` (several are `0.0.0`), usable as the base of\n> a dev prerelease.\n>\n> ### Kept private\n>\n> | Package | Path | Version | Why |\n> | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n> | (root) | `.` | n/a | Repository root. |\n> | `@endo/benchmark` | `packages/benchmark` | 0.1.4 | Benchmarks. |\n> | `@endo/chacha12-fast-check-test` | `packages/chacha12-fast-check-test` | 0.1.1 | Integration test only. |\n> | `@endo/demo` | `packages/demo` | 0.0.1 | Demo. |\n> | `@endo/eventual-send-test` | `packages/eventual-send-test` | 1.0.0 | Test-only host that breaks a devDependency cycle. |\n> | `@endo/harden-test` | `packages/harden-test` | 1.0.0 | Test-only host that breaks a devDependency cycle. |\n> | `@endo/hex-test` | `packages/hex-test` | 1.0.0 | Test-only host that breaks a devDependency cycle. |\n> | `@endo/ses-test` | `packages/ses-test` | 1.0.0 | Test-only host that breaks a devDependency cycle. |\n> | `@endo/stream-types-test` | `packages/stream-types-test` | 1.0.19 | Type tests. |\n> | `@endo/hardened262` | `packages/hardened262` | 0.1.0 | Test corpus in test262 format; no exports. |\n> | `@endo/test262-runner` | `packages/test262-runner` | 0.1.50 | Test harness; exports only `./package.json`. |\n> | `@endo/skel` | `packages/skel` | 1.1.13 | Template for new packages. |\n> | `@endo/familiar` | `packages/familiar` | 0.1.0 | Electron desktop application, built and shipped with Electron Forge, not installed from npm; no `files` list. |\n> | `@endo/floot-android` | `packages/floot-android` | 0.1.0 | Android application build; no JavaScript entry point and no dependencies. |\n>\n> After the flip, no public workspace depends at run time (`dependencies`,\n> `peerDependencies`, `optionalDependencies`) on a private one. The chains\n> noted earlier (`@endo/exo-git` → `@endo/pubsub`; `@endo/agentry` →\n> `@endo/daemon` → `@endo/daemon-cas`, `@endo/git`, `@endo/host-spawner`,\n> `@endo/ocapn-noise`, `@endo/relay-server`; `@endo/agent-tools` →\n> `@endo/exo-git`) are all public now.\n>\n> ### Release path on master\n>\n> The `master` release path is unchanged: `.github/workflows/release.yml`\n> runs only on pushes to `master`, where these workspaces stay private. On\n> `llm`, two effects to know about:\n>\n> - `scripts/release-npm.mjs` and `scripts/pack-all.mjs` select workspaces\n>   with `yarn workspaces list --no-private`, so a `release:npm` run from\n>   `llm` would now pack and publish these 55 too. CI on `llm` runs\n>   `yarn smoketest:publish`, which does that against a disposable Verdaccio,\n>   so that job now packs 55 more tarballs.\n> - `.changeset/config.json` already has `privatePackages.version` and\n>   `tag` set to true, so Changesets already versioned and tagged these\n>   workspaces while private. The change is that `changeset publish` would\n>   now publish them as well.\n>\n> ### Verification\n>\n> - `yarn test:package-uniformity`: 18 tests passed.\n>   `node scripts/check-package-uniformity.mjs`: exit 0.\n> - Prettier `--check` on every `packages/*/package.json` and the new\n>   changeset: clean.\n> - Each of the 55 flipped workspaces packs with ts-node-pack. Each\n>   tarball's `main`, `types`, `bin` and literal `exports` targets are\n>   present in it. `@endo/ocapn-noise` ships `gen/ocapn-noise.wasm` and\n>   `src/wasm/*`.\n> - `yarn pack:all` over all public workspaces: run after building `ses` (`yarn build` in `packages/ses`, since its `dist/` is a build product; CI runs `yarn build` first). It exits 0 and writes 122 tarballs, which matches the 122 workspaces `yarn workspaces list --no-private` reports.\n> - `garden prose diff 0368767`: no findings.\n\n## For the maintainer, not the pull request\n\n**Close calls, flipped:**\n\n- `@endo/chat`: a web application, but it has `main`, `exports` and\n  `files`, and it is consumed as a package, so it was flipped.\n- `@endo/thixotrope`: described as a prototype, but prototypes are not in\n  the exclusion list, and it has a `thix` bin and exports. Flipped.\n- `@endo/ironhorse-prelude`: `@endo/thixotrope` (public) depends on it at\n  run time, so it has to be public. Its `codec-polyfill.js` reads\n  `../../rust/endo/xsnap/src/polyfills.js`, which exists only inside the\n  repository. It is a build-time helper and will throw from an installed copy.\n- `@endo/goblin-chat`, `@endo/space-whylip`, `@endo/npm-registry-server`,\n  `@endo/agent-mcp-stdio`: applications or servers with exports or bins,\n  installable from npm. Flipped.\n- `@endo/test262-runner` and `@endo/hardened262`: kept private as test\n  tooling. Nothing public depends on them.\n- `@endo/familiar` and `@endo/floot-android`: kept private as application\n  shells, not npm packages. Nothing public depends on them.\n\n**Not fixed, worth knowing:**\n\n- `@endo/claude-sandbox`, `@endo/codex-sandbox` and `@endo/opencode-sandbox`\n  find `@endo/sandbox` with `new URL('../../sandbox/src/native-agent.js',\n  import.meta.url)`. From `node_modules/@endo/<pkg>/src`, that path reaches\n  `node_modules/@endo/sandbox/src/native-agent.js` only when\n  `@endo/sandbox` sits in the same `node_modules/@endo` directory. That holds\n  for a flat npm install, but not for a pnpm-style layout.\n- 19 flipped workspaces have no `files` list, so their tarballs carry\n  tests, and sometimes benchmarks, along with the code: 9p-server,\n  claude-sandbox, codex-sandbox, conversation-tree, endo-fs-asset-server,\n  endo-fs-exec, fae, floot, git, host-shell, host-spawner, hosted-agent,\n  jsonl-transcript, opencode-sandbox, reminder, space-endo-mgmt,\n  space-file-explorer, space-floot, workflow. The tarballs are usable. I did\n  not add `files` lists, because a narrow list risks dropping run-time\n  directories (for example `oci/` in the sandbox adapters), and I did not\n  have time to check each one.\n- `yarn changeset status` fails at the base itself: `.changeset/lucky-planes-resolve.md`\n  has no front matter. That predates this change.\n\n**Environment notes:** the shared bare repository failed git's\nsafe.directory check for the slot user, so `garden project add` failed until\nI wrote `safe.directory = *` into the slot's own `~/.gitconfig`. The\n`-c safe.directory=*` in `src/project.js` does not reach the upload-pack\nthat `git clone` spawns. This is probably why earlier attempts at this job\nfailed. Corepack's yarn 4.13.0 failed to start as ESM (\"Dynamic require of\nutil\"). It ran when loaded as `.cjs`. The install had no `node_modules/.bin`\nlinks, so I ran ava, prettier and changesets through `node <path>`. The\nnative better-sqlite3 build failed during install; none of the checks here\nuse it. I did not run eslint, because no JavaScript changed.\n\nI added these two workarounds as lessons in `roles/PLOT.md`.\n"
